{
  "info": {
    "name": "Integriq — endpoint response cache and problem documents (gateway-response-cache-and-problem-errors)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Newman run of openspec/changes/gateway-response-cache-and-problem-errors (REQ-RCPE-001, REQ-RCPE-002).\n\nREQ-RCPE-001: an endpoint caching GET answers for 60 seconds, in front of Nextcloud's own status.php (which sends no Cache-Control), answers the first call with `X-Cache: MISS` and the second with `X-Cache: HIT` and the same body; the source is called once and the call log marks the hit; clearing the endpoint's cache makes the next call reach the source again. A second endpoint in front of the OpenRegister API, which answers `Cache-Control: no-store`, is never answered from the cache.\n\nREQ-RCPE-002: a wrong API key on a protected endpoint is a 401 and a call to a path no endpoint serves a 404, each an `application/problem+json` document with type, title, status, detail and instance, and still the old `error` member.\n\nSetup creates the sources, the rule and the endpoints through OpenRegister, teardown deletes them. Run it with tests/postman/integriq.postman_environment.json."
  },
